# Integration Plan: Port Prediction ML Engine into Varka Platform

Integrate the existing `port_prediction--main` dry-bulk freight forecasting and vessel optimization engine into the Varka platform. This exposes real-time XGBoost 60-day freight forecasts, Open-Meteo marine wave conditions, port feasibility constraints, JIT slow-steaming decarbonization, and commercial charter strategies directly into a new **PORT FORECAST** module on the authenticated homepage.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Architecture & Security Boundaries**:
> - **Python FastAPI ML Service** runs on `http://127.0.0.1:8000` loading models and datasets once at startup.
> - **Node.js Express Backend** (`http://localhost:3030`) acts as the secure gateway, protecting all prediction APIs with the existing `authMiddleware`.
> - **Next.js Frontend** (`http://localhost:3000`) calls only `http://localhost:3030/api/v1/prediction/*` and never connects directly to Python.
> - **Zero Synthetic/Faked APIs**: The forecast, drivers, feasibility, JIT savings, and marine wave data strictly call the real Python engine and live Open-Meteo APIs.

