## Proposed Changes

### 1. Python FastAPI Microservice (`port_prediction--main/`)

#### [NEW] [port_prediction--main/api/main.py](file:///c:/github/varka/varka/port_prediction--main/api/main.py)
- FastAPI application running on `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.
- Loads the 29.8 MB timeseries dataset, ports, vessels, and routes **once at startup** into an in-memory cache to guarantee high API performance.
- Endpoints:
  - `GET /health`: Health status.
  - `GET /api/v1/routes`: Returns list of origins, destinations, vessels, and valid route mappings.
  - `GET /api/v1/predict/forecast`: Executes the existing `forecast_route` XGBoost model for a given `route_id` and `vessel` with 60-day horizon, returning `current_rate_usd_t`, `uncertainty_band_usd_t`, `outlook` (P10, P90, projected rates), and `drivers` (feature impacts).
  - `GET /api/v1/live/marine`: Calls `marine_risk(port_code)` in `live_data.py` to retrieve real-time wave height, wind-wave height, and sea risk level from Open-Meteo.
  - `POST /api/v1/plan/jit`: Calls `just_in_time_plan` to calculate slow-steaming speed, hours avoided at anchorage, fuel saved (MT), and CO₂ emissions reduced.
  - `POST /api/v1/optimize/vessel`: Calls `feasible` and `optimize_vessels` to check draft, LOA, beam, and DWT utilization across origin & destination.
  - `POST /api/v1/strategy/charter`: Calls `recommend_strategy` to generate contract scenario recommendations (1, 3, 6-voyage coverage).

